// Mishearing corrections for spoken engineering English, generated by
// gen_corrections.py from the cleaned chemical-engineering glossary
// bundle (corrections.json for the certain pairs, slash-pairs.json for
// the uncertain pairs, words.txt and traps.txt for the dictionary
// pass — the same bundle the Muse transcription skill uses).
// Do not edit by hand: regenerate. Pairs are ordered longest heard form
// first; matching is case-insensitive at word boundaries, in a single pass
// over the original text, so text inserted by a correction is never
// rescanned. Each pair carries a class: "certain" pairs replace the heard
// form with the term; "slash" pairs are uncertain (the class is data
// from the cleaned bundle: an ordinary-word heard form, or several
// candidate terms) and the transcript shows the heard form followed by
// every candidate, slash-separated with no spaces.
// Boundaries are letter/digit lookarounds, not \b, so heard forms
// ending in a non-word character (a parenthesis, a bracket, an
// ellipsis) can still match. A certain pair whose term only extends
// the heard form does not apply when the text already continues with
// the term's own continuation, and a pair that would not change the
// text is not logged as a correction.
// For a slash pair with several candidates, context can settle the
// choice: if the word right after the heard form is the last word of
// exactly one candidate (or the word right before is the first word of
// exactly one), that candidate replaces outright, the cue word is
// absorbed, and the application is logged as context-chosen.
// After the pairs, a dictionary pass looks for words that are in
// neither the bundled English wordlist (SCOWL) nor the technical
// vocabulary and matches them against the technical terms on sound
// (Soundex) and spelling (edit distance) under a calibrated bar; its
// replacements carry the kind "dictionary". A mechanical tidy-up
// (fillers, duplicate words, spacing, capitalisation) runs last.
// Most pairs are predicted sound-alikes, not attested errors; the page
// lists every correction it applies so over-corrections are visible.
